            </profile>
            <profile id="4582-d3d0-f0dc-f196" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="eb14-e889-c793-0fc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Armed with a sword. May have light armour (+3 pts), shield (+2 pts), large shield (+4 pts) if on foot. May ride a horse (free) - his Movement rate increases to 8. May be Stubborn (+3 pts). Stealth. Hates Romans. Looting. (Eg Crixus, Castus and Gannicus.) You must include at least one character to command the army. If you do not select Spartacus, or he is not available, a Heroic or Tribal leader may be made the General (+45 pts) and have their Ld raised to 9 or 7 respectively. (Spartacus p.13)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="75d6-98f4-916a-5f76" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="6+">
