            <profile id="fcdb-555f-f788-408e" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="eb14-e889-c793-0fc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Armed with a hand weapon. May have light armour (+2 pts), and shield (+1 pt) or large shield (+2 pts). May be armed with one of the following: additional hand weapon (+2 pts), throwing spear (+2 pts), pilum (+4 pts), or double-handed weapon (+3 pts). May increase Toughness to 4 (+5 pts). May be made Stubborn (+3 pts). Stealth. Hates Romans. Looting. Different Equipment. Up to eight Gladiators per 1,000 points (Early and Late armies; up to five in the Germano-Gallic army), pro rata rounding down. Upon deployment the player may deploy the Gladiators as a single unit of Light Infantry (at least five models, no Leader, Musician or Standard) or include them within other units to a maximum of two per unit; if deployed in other units they are subject to that unit's Leadership and psychology and may not leave. If joined by Spartacus the unit is immune to panic, fear and terror and may use his Leadership even in skirmish order. Victory points are gained for each Gladiator killed. (The option choices are per unit here; the book allows each Gladiator model to be armed differently.) (Spartacus p.13)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="5b30-f6a6-bdbf-4f36" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
