  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ef10-cc49-0f73-89a1" name="Spartacus's Slave Revolt (Spartacus) - List Notes" publicationId="eb14-e889-c793-0fc4" hidden="false">
      <description>SPARTACUS'S SLAVE REVOLT (Spartacus, pp.12-14). The minimum size of a unit is five infantry models or five cavalry models, with no upper limit; one model in each unit may be upgraded to a Leader (+5 pts), Standard Bearer (+5 pts) and Musician (+5 pts) unless mentioned otherwise. Special rules: HATE ROMANS: subject to the Hatred rules sections 2 and 3 but not 1 (re-roll misses in the first round of combat and must pursue towards Roman units). LOOTING: a Slave unit catching and destroying a fleeing Roman unit better equipped with shields and weapons may loot the bodies and continue the battle using that equipment instead (it does not include armour); if the Slave unit subsequently flees it loses the bonus equipment. LEADERSHIP &amp; WARBAND PSYCHOLOGY: if a character that does not have Warband psychology joins a unit with Warband psychology, the unit must use either its own Ld or the character's Ld and add on the Warband rank bonus. STEALTH: may move through difficult ground and obstacles at a normal pace even if formed, but lose combat rank bonuses when fighting in difficult ground or across obstacles; may not march; must see their foe before charging. FIERY ROLLERS (0-1, 40 pts): one formed unit of Gladiators, Trained, Gallic or Germanic Slaves carries two rollers; it causes fear in its frontal facing; it may only move in open terrain; in its Shooting phase it may 'shoot' one or both rollers at an enemy unit (3D6" from higher ground, 2D6" on level ground, over clear ground); a roller reaching the enemy causes D6 Strength 4 hits with no armour save (Drilled units and skirmishers take a Ld test at -1 to avoid each); if the unit is charged to its front or charges, each roller causes D6 S4 hits; the rollers can only be used once.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Spartacus's Slave Revolt - Early Revolt Army]
  Characters: up to 30%
  Slave Infantry: at least 25%
  Gallic and Germanic Slaves: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Cavalry: up to 15%
  Artillery: up to 100%
  Commanded by Spartacus before the Gauls and Germans under Crixus split off (also the army Spartacus commanded between Crixus's death and the last separation of the Gauls and Germans). Characters up to 30% (may include Spartacus and up to eight Gladiators per 1,000 pts); Slave Infantry at least 25% and at least 25% and up to 50% of the points must be spent on Gallic and Germanic Slaves; Cavalry up to 15%; Artillery one looted piece per 2,000 pts.
[Spartacus's Slave Revolt - Germano-Gallic Slave Army]
  Characters: up to 30%
  Slave Infantry: at least 50%
  Gallic and Germanic Slaves: at least 50%
  Cavalry: up to 10%
  The Germano-Gallic force that split off from the main slave army, first under Crixus then later commanded by Castus and Gannicus. Characters up to 30% (Spartacus may not be taken; up to five Gladiators per 1,000 pts); at least 50% of the points must be spent on Gallic and Germanic slaves (Slave Infantry at least 50%); may not take any Trained Slaves; Slave Cavalry up to 10%; no Artillery.
[Spartacus's Slave Revolt - Late Revolt Army]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Slave Infantry: at least 50%
  Gallic and Germanic Slaves: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 20%
  Commanded by Spartacus in his last battles against the Romans. Characters up to 25% (may take Spartacus and up to eight Gladiators per 1,000 pts); Slave Infantry at least 50% (up to 25% of the army may be Gallic or Germanic Slaves); Slave Cavalry up to 20%; Artillery one looted piece per 1,000 pts.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
